.TH MANARADIX 1 "2026-08-14" "manaradix 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
manaradix \- Btrfs snapshot, subvolume, and filesystem management utility for Mageia
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B manaradix
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B manaradix
provides a unified graphical and text interface for managing Btrfs
snapshots, subvolumes, and filesystem parameters on Mageia 10 and
Cauldron.  It is built on top of python-manatools using the aui
(Abstract UI) backend, so a single codebase renders in Qt, GTK, and
ncurses frontends.

With no subcommand,
.B manaradix
launches the GUI.  The GUI always re-executes via pkexec (polkit) so
snapshot operations work from a normal user session.

Subcommands run headless and are suitable for scripts and systemd
service units:
.B snapshot
(create, list, delete, prune, info),
.B setup
(status, apply, list-profiles),
.B activity
(status, record),
.B dbus
(serve, status), and
.B tray
(serve, status) \-\- the notification-area applet, a user-session
process that watches filesystem health and snapshot retention and
notifies about problems (see
.BR manaradix-config (5),
.IR "[tray]" ).

All destructive operations support
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to the configuration file (default:
.IR /etc/manaradix/config.toml ).
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot\-dir \fIDIR\fR
Snapshot storage directory relative to the mount point (default:
.IR .snapshots ).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.B \-\-frontend \fI{\fRqt\fR,\fRgtk\fR,\fRncurses\fR}\fR
UI toolkit frontend (default: auto-detect; qt/gtk fall back to
ncurses).  Only meaningful in GUI mode.  Maps to the
.B MUI_BACKEND
environment variable understood by python-manatools.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS snapshot
Snapshot lifecycle and retention pruning.
.TP
.B manaradix snapshot create
[\fB\-\-subvolume\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
[\fB\-\-schedule\fR \fIS\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-read\-write\fR] [\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]

Create a snapshot.  \fB\-\-subvolume\fR is the source subvolume path
(default
.IR / ).
\fB\-\-type\fR selects the snapshot type: \fBmanual\fR (default),
\fBreadonly\fR, \fBtimed\fR, \fBboot\fR, \fBpre\-restore\fR,
\fBpre\-install\fR, or \fBpre\-upgrade\fR.  \fB\-\-schedule\fR tags the
snapshot with a retention tier (\fBhourly\fR, \fBdaily\fR, \fBweekly\fR,
\fBmonthly\fR, \fBboot\fR, \fBpre\-upgrade\fR); it is only meaningful
with \fB\-\-type timed\fR or \fB\-\-type pre\-upgrade\fR.  Snapshots are
read-only by default; \fB\-\-read\-write\fR creates a writable one.

When \fB\-\-type pre\-upgrade\fR is requested but
.B snapshot_before_upgrade
is disabled in the configuration, the command silently does nothing and
exits 0.
.TP
.B manaradix snapshot list
[\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-subvolume\fR \fIPATH\fR]

List snapshots for a mount point (default
.IR / ),
optionally filtered by source subvolume.
.TP
.B manaradix snapshot info
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR]

Show details of one snapshot.  \fIID\fR is the snapshot timestamp, e.g.
.IR 2026\-01\-15_14\-00\-00 .
.TP
.B manaradix snapshot delete
\fB\-\-id\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]

Delete a snapshot and its metadata.
.TP
.B manaradix snapshot prune
\fB\-\-subvolume\fR \fIPATH\fR \fB\-\-schedule\fR \fIS\fR
[\fB\-\-mount\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]

Keep the N most recent snapshots for the given schedule tier, N coming
from the retention policy in the configuration, and delete the rest.
This is the command invoked by the generated systemd timer units; it
warns and exits 0 if no policy is configured for the subvolume.
.SS setup
First-run setup wizard (headless).
.TP
.B manaradix setup status

Report whether the recommended setup is still needed (no snapshots and
no policies), the detected role, and the default profile.  Read-only.
.TP
.B manaradix setup list\-profiles

List the available setup profiles.  Read-only.
.TP
.B manaradix setup apply
[\fB\-\-profile\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]

Apply a setup profile (global configuration, per-subvolume policies,
systemd units, GRUB script as the layout permits).  \fB\-\-profile\fR
selects the profile (desktop, server, kiosk, or a custom template id);
it defaults to the profile detected for this system.  Elevated via
pkexec.
.SS activity
Automated snapshot activity status and run records.
.TP
.B manaradix activity status
[\fB\-\-subvolume\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-schedule\fR \fIS\fR]

Report per-activity status: state, last run, result.  Read-only, never
elevated.
.TP
.B manaradix activity record
\fB\-\-subvolume\fR \fIPATH\fR \fB\-\-schedule\fR \fIS\fR
[\fB\-\-result\fR \fI{\fRsuccess\fR,\fRfailed\fR,\fRcancelled\fR,\fRunknown\fR}\fR]
[\fB\-\-exit\-status\fR \fIN\fR]

Append a run record.  Invoked by the generated systemd service units
(ExecStopPost), which run as root; manual unprivileged calls fail
without an auth prompt.  \fB\-\-result\fR defaults to the
.B SERVICE_RESULT
environment variable set by systemd, \fB\-\-exit\-status\fR to
.BR EXIT_STATUS .
.SS dbus
System D-Bus service.
.TP
.B manaradix dbus serve

Run the system D-Bus service (org.mageia.manaradix) in the foreground.
Root only — exits 1 otherwise.  Normally the service is bus-activated
on demand and this command is only used by the systemd unit
.BR manaradix-dbus.service .
Exits 1 if the bus name is already taken; shuts down cleanly on SIGTERM.
.TP
.B manaradix dbus status

Report whether the service is running, without activating it (checks
the bus name owner).  Prints
.B running
and exits 0, or prints a hint and exits 2.
.SS tray
Notification-area applet (user session, session bus).
.TP
.B manaradix tray serve

Run the tray applet in the foreground.  Starts automatically at login
from
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart/manaradix-tray.desktop .
Exits 0 immediately when the applet is disabled in the configuration,
when no StatusNotifierWatcher is present (no tray-capable desktop), or
when another instance already owns
.IR org.mageia.manaradix.Tray .
Checks run on a worker thread and report through the D-Bus daemon; the
applet itself never elevates.  Shuts down cleanly on SIGTERM/SIGINT.
.TP
.B manaradix tray status

Report whether the applet is running, without activating it (checks the
session-bus name owner).  Prints a confirmation and exits 0, or prints
a hint and exits 2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.  Includes the documented no-ops: pre-upgrade snapshots with
the feature disabled, and pruning with no policy configured.
.TP
.B 1
Operation failure, pkexec unavailable or failed, daemon refused (not
root, bus name taken), GUI startup failure.
.TP
.B 2
.B dbus status
or
.B tray status
when the respective service is not running.  (argparse usage errors
also exit 2; \fB\-\-help\fR exits 0.)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MUI_BACKEND
UI backend selection (\fBqt\fR, \fBgtk\fR, \fBncurses\fR), understood
by python-manatools.
.TP
.B MANARADIX_PKEXEC
Set on the re-executed process to prevent pkexec elevation loops.
.TP
.B MANARADIX_TEMPLATE_DIRS
Colon-separated search path for setup profile templates.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/manaradix/config.toml
Configuration (see
.BR manaradix-config (5)).
.TP
.I /usr/share/manaradix/templates/
Shipped setup profiles (TOML).
.TP
.I /etc/manaradix/templates.d/
Administrator template overrides and extras.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR manaradix-config (5),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR dbus-daemon (1)
